WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.460
Measure, plan, light, and calculate curtain fabric.

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:10.770
This is the video for module two of Interior Decoration Basics: measure, plan, light and dress the room.

3
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:20.850
Most expensive decorating mistakes are measuring mistakes. A sofa that will not pass through the door. Curtains 20 cm too short.

4
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.010
And one bright bulb in the centre of the ceiling is why many rooms feel flat at night.

5
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:35.020
This video turns your ideas into numbers: a floor plan, a lighting plan, and exact fabric metres.

6
00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:47.190
You need a 5 m or 8 m steel tape, graph paper and a pencil. Stand in the doorway and draw a rough outline. Mark the door, windows, sockets and anything fixed.

7
00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:54.160
Start at one corner and work clockwise. Measure each wall along the floor, in centimetres.

8
00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:02.130
Measure each window and door, and draw the curve of the door swing. Furniture cannot sit inside that curve.

9
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:12.210
Opposite walls should be nearly the same. If one is 360 cm and the opposite is 342, measure both again.

10
00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:28.720
Now draw at a scale of 1:50. Divide every measurement in centimetres by 50. Chiamaka's bedroom of 420 by 360 cm becomes 8.4 by 7.2 cm on paper.

11
00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:38.930
Cut out furniture at the same scale and slide it around. Keep main walkways about 90 cm, and never block doors, sockets or windows.

12
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.940
Professionals plan light in layers. Ambient light fills the room so people can move safely.

13
00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:53.910
Task light is brighter, for a job: a reading lamp, a desk lamp for homework, a light over the kitchen counter.

14
00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:05.290
Accent light creates mood: a small table lamp, or a strip light behind the TV. One lamp in a dark corner often does more than a brighter ceiling bulb.

15
00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:18.660
With LED bulbs, compare lumens. About 800 lumens gives roughly the light of an old 60 W bulb, using far less power, which matters on an inverter or generator.

16
00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:31.580
Warm white, about 2700 to 3000 K, suits living rooms and bedrooms. For power cuts, put one light on the inverter circuit or use rechargeable lamps.

17
00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:50.190
Aisha's client has a 1.8 m track, 2.4 m above the floor, for floor-length pencil pleat curtains. First, the cut drop: the finished drop plus about 30 cm for heading and hem. 2.4 plus 0.3 is 2.7 m.

18
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:59.250
Pencil pleat curtains need about twice the track width, so 1.8 times 2 is 3.6 m of fabric across.

19
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:09.760
The fabric is 1.4 m wide. 3.6 divided by 1.4 is 2.57, so round up to 3 widths.

20
00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:22.570
3 widths times 2.7 m is 8.1 m. Patterned fabric needs more, because each drop is rounded up to whole pattern repeats. Tell the client before they choose.

21
00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:29.710
Now the cost. These prices are only for illustration. Check current prices at your market.

22
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:35.200
If the fabric sells for about 4,000 naira per metre,

23
00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:49.020
then 8.1 m is about 32,400 naira, before lining, tape and tailoring. Many people round up to 8.5 m, in case of shrinkage or a cutting mistake.

24
00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:58.800
When measuring high up, use a stable step ladder on a flat floor, never a plastic chair. Have someone hold it, and switch off ceiling fans.

25
00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:10.480
Never do wiring yourself. Use a qualified electrician for new points and inverter connections. Do not overload sockets, and do not run cables under rugs.

26
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:20.120
Keep curtains and throws away from cookers, candles, mosquito coils and hot bulbs, and keep blind cords out of children's reach.

27
00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:38.440
To remember. Measure clockwise in centimetres and draw at 1:50. Keep walkways about 90 cm. Plan ambient, task and accent light. Widths equal track times fullness, divided by fabric width. Always round up, and allow more for patterns.

28
00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:53.320
Now practise. Draw one room to scale and try two layouts with cut-outs. Map the light in a room and mark where a task and an accent light should go. And calculate curtains for a real window, plain and patterned.

29
00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.610
Continue with the lessons below.
